# Sygg's Command, modes 1 and 2: "Create a token that's a copy of target Merfolk you control" and "Creatures target player controls gain
# lifelink until end of turn". Bot1 controls a Coral Merfolk and an Ornithopter, Bot2 its own Coral Merfolk. Refused for the copy: Bot2's
# Merfolk (not "you control") and Bot1's Ornithopter (not a Merfolk). Modes happen in printed order (CR 700.2d) and the lifelink takes the
# creatures there are as it resolves (CR 611.2c), so the token copy has it too, as do the Merfolk and the Ornithopter; Bot2's Merfolk does
# not. Bot1's Merfolk attacks for 2 and gains 2 life.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Coral Merfolk
Sygg's Command
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Coral Merfolk
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Coral Merfolk.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Coral Merfolk.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sygg's Command.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1; 2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk#2.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk#2.Keywords = Lifelink
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Lifelink
? Bot2.Battlefield.Coral Merfolk.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Attack(Coral Merfolk#1 > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot2.Life = 18
